# Groovebox v4 — Exhaustive Product, Performance, Musicality & Technical Specification (`groovebox4.md`)

## 1. Product Vision, Dual-Persona Modes & Target Hardware
* **Product Concept:** A self-contained, 100% browser-based, all-synth 8-track groovebox, extendable-note step sequencer, live clip-launching performance workstation, expressive pad controller, modular-style synthesizer, internal resampler, and song arranger engineered for both touchscreen tablets and desktop workstations.
* **Dual-Mode Architecture (`BEGINNER / PLAY` vs. `PRO / STUDIO`):**
  * **Seamless Mode Toggle in Top Transport Bar:** Flips the UI and DSP depth instantaneously without reloading or breaking compatibility.
  * **Shared Underlying Audio Engine:** Both modes run on the exact same pure TypeScript Web Audio synthesis engine. Patches and songs created in **Pro (`STUDIO`) Mode** can be opened and played in **Beginner (`PLAY`) Mode** (where the 6 beginner macro sliders map to weighted combinations of the Pro synth parameters), and vice versa.
  * **Persona 1 — `BEGINNER (PLAY)` Mode (7-Year-Old Ergonomics):** Tactile Teenage Engineering / Ableton Note / Nintendo Labo aesthetic; bold per-track color coding, 6 large visual-level macro faders per track with dual-layer friendly labels + micro-icons, reactive oscilloscope, draggable ADSR mountain, functional note color-coding, simplified 1-bar quantized live remix pads, one-tap musical co-play tools (`ANSWER ME`, `MAGIC CHORD`), and parent-protected `SAFE LOCK` mode.
  * **Persona 2 — `PRO (STUDIO)` Mode (Adult Producer / High-Spec Tablet or PC):** Unlocks full multi-oscillator analog/hybrid synthesis (**2 Primary Oscillators + 2 Sub-Oscillators + Noise**), Voice Modes (`Mono / Legato / Poly / Unison`), Portamento/Glide, Oscillator Key-Sync, 3 independent envelopes, dual LFOs, drag-and-drop **8-Slot Modulation Matrix**, **16-Step Modulation Sequencer**, **Per-Channel Insert FX Chains (with Sidechain & Transient Shaper)**, **Per-Track Stereo Width & Sub Mono-Maker**, **Master Bus Mastering Chain**, **Per-Note Visual Velocity & Micro-Timing Lanes**, **Euclidean Rhythms & Conditional Trigs**, **`PERFORMANCE` Live Clip Launch Matrix & Dual-Deck `A/B` Pattern Crossfader**, **Scene Crossfader**, **Internal Resampling**, **Web MIDI I/O + `.mid` Export**, and **8-Track `.wav` Stem Export**.
* **Target Hardware Tiers:**
  * **Tier 1 (Beginner / Portable Tablet):** **Lenovo Tab 6** ($1920 \times 1200$ 10.3" landscape IPS, Qualcomm Snapdragon 690, 4GB RAM, native $48000\text{ Hz}$ audio output via 3.5mm wired headphone jack). Includes an **`ECO` Performance Toggle** (30fps canvas throttling, shared algorithmic comb-filter reverb, $160\text{ ms}$ lookahead buffer, strict one-shot node garbage collection) so mid-range mobile CPUs never stutter.
  * **Tier 2 (Pro / Studio Workstation):** **Windows/macOS PC or High-Spec Tablet** (e.g., Galaxy Tab S9/S10, iPad Pro). Runs at 60fps with full polyphony/unison, active per-channel insert FX chains, audio-rate modulation, QWERTY keyboard shortcuts, and Web MIDI hardware integration.
* **Distribution & Packaging:** Client-side **Progressive Web App (PWA)** (`manifest.json` + Service Worker for 100% offline use) and Android **Trusted Web Activity (TWA)** locked to landscape (`100vw` by `100dvh`, zero page scrolling).

