## 2. Technology Stack & Core Audio Engineering Mandates
* **Core Language:** **TypeScript** (strict mode) for all state, DSP voice graphs, lookahead scheduling, per-track clip routing, parameter addressing, and UI components.
* **UI & Visualizers:** **React 18+** + **Vite** + **Tailwind CSS**, paired with high-DPI **HTML5 `<canvas>`** (`requestAnimationFrame`) for the zero-crossing oscilloscope, FFT spectrum, ADSR/filter curves, Kaoss X/Y trails, velocity/micro-timing lanes, and LED VU meters.
* **Audio Engine:** Native **Web Audio API** (`AudioContext`, `OscillatorNode`, `BiquadFilterNode`, `GainNode`, `WaveShaperNode`, `DelayNode`, `DynamicsCompressorNode`, `StereoPannerNode`, `AnalyserNode`, `OfflineAudioContext`), plus **`AudioWorklet`** processors for custom bitcrushing, sample-rate reduction, tape wow/flutter, and analog wavefolding.
* **Hardware Integration & Persistence:** **Web MIDI API** (`navigator.requestMIDIAccess`), **`IndexedDB`** (`idb` + `navigator.storage.persist()`), `.json` project I/O, `.mid` Standard MIDI File export, and `.wav` stereo/stem/resampled audio export.

### Critical Real-Time Performance Rules
1. **Strictly Decouple Audio & Scheduler from React State:**
   * **NEVER** trigger React `useState` updates on step ticks, 60fps VU meter reads, or continuous fader drags.
   * Keep the audio graph, lookahead scheduler, active clip routing pointers, and active parameter values in pure TypeScript modules outside React. Update playhead highlights and clip launch status indicators via direct DOM class toggling and `<canvas>` loops, syncing to React only on pointer release or structural edits.
2. **Sample-Accurate Lookahead Scheduler with Extendable Gate & Per-Track Clip Routing:**
   * A timer ($25\text{ ms}$ to $40\text{ ms}$ interval) inspects `audioContext.currentTime` and schedules note triggers, gate-off releases, and parameter ramps **$100\text{ ms}$ to $160\text{ ms}$ ahead** using exact Web Audio timestamps (`osc.start(tStart)` and `gateOff(tEnd)`), with catch-up protection against main-thread stalls.
   * **Zero-Overhead Per-Track Clip Pointer Routing:** Because all patterns (`A1–D4`) reside in memory as lightweight JSON step arrays, routing Track 1 to read from Pattern `B2` while Track 5 reads from Pattern `A1` requires **zero extra DSP voices or RAM**—the scheduler simply resolves `activePatternForTrack[trackIndex]` on each step boundary.
   * **Multi-Step Gate Lifecycle:** For notes with `durationSteps > 1`, `Gate On` triggers Attack $\rightarrow$ Decay $\rightarrow$ Sustain at `tStart`, holds the Sustain level across the spanned steps, and schedules `Gate Off` (Release) at $t_{\text{end}} = t_{\text{start}} + (\text{durationSteps} \times \text{stepDuration})$. Overlapping or adjacent tied notes engage true Legato pitch glide without re-triggering envelopes from zero.
3. **Native Hardware Sample Rate ($48\text{ kHz}$):**
   * Initialize `new AudioContext({ latencyHint: 'interactive' })` without forcing $44100\text{ Hz}$ so Chrome/Android runs natively at $48000\text{ Hz}$ without resampling overhead.
4. **Auto-Resume Watchdog, Latency Detection & Node Lifecycle Hygiene:**
   * Attach `onstatechange` and user-gesture resume listeners so sandboxed/mobile browsers never leave the `AudioContext` suspended, and disconnect all one-shot percussion nodes via `onended` + fallback timers.
   * Monitor `audioContext.outputLatency` and display a gentle tip recommending wired headphones if Bluetooth latency exceeds $80\text{ ms}$.
5. **CPU Voice Pooling & Idle Bypass:**
   * Any oscillator or sub-oscillator whose mixer level is $0\%$ is bypassed/muted so it consumes zero CPU. Melodic tracks use pooled voice graphs with smooth parameter transitions (`AudioParam.setTargetAtTime()`).

